---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const steps = [
  {
    label: "The problem",
    body: "Farmers don't just lack money. They lack the right money at the right time, tied to the right support: capital before sowing, when the income only lands after harvest; feed today, when the milk pays out tomorrow. Meanwhile the people with money to put to work want in, but they can't tell which farmer to trust, can't watch the fields from the city, and fear the fraud and the blame if a season fails. So the real gap isn't only capital. It's trust.",
  },
  {
    label: "Who it's for",
    body: "The people who grow everyone's food and get served last by everyone's banks. I'm not interested in another loan app dressing up the same old extraction. I want to make the farmer and the investor legible to each other, honestly, and do it without bulldozing the local relationships that already hold these places together. My people first. Fairness as the architecture, not the marketing.",
  },
  {
    label: "The shape",
    body: "A trust-and-operations layer between three people: the farmer who needs seasonal capital and a hand executing, the investor who needs proof and a real downside, and the local operator who actually knows the ground. Money tied to a specific use. Verified locally before anyone funds it. Tracked through the season. Repaid through a real event: milk at the collection centre, produce at the buyer, grain at the mandi. Start manual, a ledger and field visits and a phone, and earn the right to become software later. Not a loan app. Infrastructure.",
  },
];

const prove = [
  "Farmers will take outside capital, if a trusted local face introduces it.",
  "Investors will fund a farm, if the ask is specific, verified, and reported like it's real.",
  "A local operator can verify and monitor without quietly becoming the next middleman.",
  "Repayment can hang on a real cash-flow event, not a promise.",
  "The farmer walks away feeling helped, not trapped.",
];
---
<BaseLayout title="A farmer capital network · Sundharesan Kumaresan" description="A trusted network where capital and logistics reach farmers directly. The whole thing rests on trust.">
  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto max-w-[1100px] px-6 pt-16 pb-16">
    <a href="/to" class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-text-muted transition-colors hover:text-text">&larr; To</a>
    <p class="mt-6 font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">A venture</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-serif font-semibold leading-[0.98]" style="font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 6.5vw, 4rem);">A farmer capital network</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-[60ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-muted">A trusted network where capital reaches farmers directly, on terms that fit how a farm actually works: timely money, logistics, inputs, and a real route to market. Across crops, dairy, and the seasons in between.</p>
    <p class="mt-8 max-w-[30ch] font-serif font-semibold leading-[1.08]" style="font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3.8vw, 2.25rem);">Capital and logistics are the work. <span class="text-accent">Trust</span> is the ground it all stands on.</p>

    <section class="mt-14" style="max-width: var(--measure)">
      <ol class="relative border-l border-border pl-8">
        {steps.map((s) => (
          <li class="relative pb-10 last:pb-0">
            <span class="absolute -left-[37px] top-1.5 h-3 w-3 rounded-full bg-stellar"></span>
            <h2 class="font-serif font-semibold leading-[1.1]" style="font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 3vw, 1.6rem);">{s.label}</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">{s.body}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-20" style="max-width: var(--measure)">
      <h2 class="font-serif font-semibold" style="font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3.4vw, 1.95rem);">Where I'd start</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">The shortest, most verifiable loop wins. Dairy feed and cattle finance, where the milk pays back daily, or logistics finance tied to one known buyer. Prove repayment and honest reporting in one narrow loop, then earn the right to do seasonal crop finance. Ninety days, fifty farmers, one geography, one trusted local partner. No grand launch.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-20">
      <h2 class="font-serif font-semibold" style="font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3.4vw, 1.95rem);">What I'd prove first</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[60ch] text-text-muted">None of it starts with software. It starts with five assumptions that have to hold:</p>
      <ul class="mt-6 border-t border-border" style="max-width: var(--measure)">
        {prove.map((p) => (
          <li class="border-b border-border py-4 text-text-muted">{p}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-[60ch] text-text-muted">If those don't hold, the app doesn't matter. So I'd test them before writing a line of it.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="mt-16" style="max-width: var(--measure)">
      <a href="/to" class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-text-muted transition-colors hover:text-text">&larr; To</a>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
